   "body": "I implemented this in my fork: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/33c0ade7a\n\nThe expanded Usage request now loads its existing routing trace and lists the actual attempts in order, with provider/model, status, duration and any recorded error. This also covers client-canceled 499 requests; an expired or unavailable trace is reported as unavailable rather than inferred from the current group configuration. No routing or retry behavior changes.\n\nVerified the Usage detail tests in Chromium and WebKit, including English and Chinese, a canceled request with multiple attempts, and unavailable history. The canceled-request test fails against the original page. Vet and builds passed on Linux and Windows; the full nogui test suite has unrelated failures in TestAgyShell and TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink and is still running.\n",
